faq:
  - q: How does the pack comparison calculator work?
    a: Enter the price and number of units in each pack. The calculator divides the price by the number of units and compares the resulting unit prices.
  - q: What is the price per unit?
    a: The price per unit is the total price of a pack divided by the number of units it contains. It allows you to compare products sold in different pack sizes.
  - q: Can I compare packs with different quantities?
    a: Yes. Comparing different pack sizes is one of the main purposes of this calculator.
  - q: Is the larger pack always cheaper?
    a: No. A larger pack may have a higher or lower price per unit. Comparing the unit price is a simple way to check which option offers better value.
  - q: Can I use it for food and groceries?
    a: Yes. You can compare food, drinks, cleaning products, toiletries or any other products sold in packs or multiple units.

